    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0300" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150 Barred Zones/6–1645</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 107</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-16">June 16,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received June 27.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that the approval of the House Immigration Committee of the Indian Immigration
                    Bill has received small but favorable press notices here. Were it not for the
                    preoccupation of the press over the Wavell Plan,<anchor n="93" xml:id="d167-f1"
                    /> the Immigration Bill would undoubtedly have received much more attention.</p>
                <p>All papers mentioned that Mr. Phillips<anchor n="94" xml:id="d167-f2"/> had
                    testified before the Committee in favor of the bill and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawn</hi><anchor n="95" xml:id="d167-f3"/> captioned its Reuters’
                    announcement “William Phillips Supports Indian Immigration Bill.”</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Merrell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d167-f1" n="93" xml:id="d167-f1-content">
                <p>Proposals concerning the future government of India made at New Delhi on June 14
                    by the Governor-General and Viceroy of India, Viscount Wavell; see British Cmd.
                    6652, <hi rendition="#italic">India: Statement of the Policy of His Majesty’s
                        Government made by the Secretary of State for India on June 14th, 1945;</hi>
                    see also <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg249">pp. 249</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d167-f2" n="94" xml:id="d167-f2-content">
                <p>William Phillips, Special Assistant to the Secretary of State, and formerly
                    Personal Representative of President Roosevelt to India; for documentation
                    regarding the Phillips mission to India, see <ref target="frus1943v04#pg_178">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, pp. 178</ref> ff., and <ref
                        target="frus1944v05#pg_232">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >v</hi>, pp. 232</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d167-f3" n="95" xml:id="d167-f3-content">
                <p>Moslem League newspaper.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
